++{"fact":{"at":"2026-09-28T15:28:00-05:00","id":"if-the-css-selector-already-starts-with-","text":"If the CSS selector already starts with the module's class (e.g., .panel { ... .grip { } }), re-prefixing to .panel-grip is optional (the nesting provides the namespace). This is a guideline, not a rule.","certainty":"open"}}
++{"fact":{"at":"2026-09-28T15:28:00-05:00","id":"the-css-census-includes-vendored-bundles","text":"The CSS census includes vendored bundles (e.g., minified three.js), so a grep hit does not always mean a collision. Look at WHERE the hit is and read the line; vendored code is no veto.","certainty":"likely"}}
++{"fact":{"at":"2026-09-28T15:28:00-05:00","id":"a-bare-line-in-css-scopes-txt-flex-card-","text":"A bare line in css-scopes.txt (.flex, .card, .pad) reserves that exact class name AND any suffixed variant (.flex-*, .card-*, .pad-*); nothing else may use those names","certainty":"settled"}}
++{"fact":{"at":"2026-09-28T15:28:00-05:00","id":"a-line-ending-with-a-dash-ui-panel-page-","text":"A line ending with a dash (ui-, panel-, page-) reserves a namespace for that module; new classes there are .prefix-<thing>, not bare or with different prefixes","certainty":"settled"}}
